From: pat <pi3iman@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: mtk_eth_soc: build datapath objects with -O2

This kernel is built with CONFIG_CC_OPTIMIZE_FOR_SIZE (-Os).  On the
in-order dual Cortex-A53 (MT7622) the datapath hot loops pay for -Os's
reduced instruction scheduling and unrolling with no OoO window to hide
it.  Compile the two objects that carry the per-packet CPU path with
-O2:

- mtk_eth_soc.o: mtk_start_xmit, TX/RX NAPI polls, ring handling
- mtk_ppe.o: __mtk_ppe_check_skb, FOE entry commit (runs for every
  unbound/slow-path packet)

mtk_wed.o is deliberately excluded (control/attach/reset only on WED
v1 — no per-packet software path), as are mtk_ppe_offload.o and the
debugfs/path objects (per-flow setup and management plane).

Per-object CFLAGS_$@ is appended after KBUILD_CFLAGS, so -O2 overrides
the global -Os (last flag wins).

Signed-off-by: pat <pi3iman@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/Makefile | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/Makefile
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/Makefile
@@ -5,6 +5,11 @@

 obj-$(CONFIG_NET_MEDIATEK_SOC) += mtk_eth.o
 mtk_eth-y := mtk_eth_soc.o mtk_eth_path.o mtk_ppe.o mtk_ppe_debugfs.o mtk_ppe_offload.o
+
+# Per-packet datapath: keep hot objects at -O2 on -Os kernels (in-order
+# A53 can't hide -Os's weaker scheduling in the xmit/NAPI/PPE-check loops)
+CFLAGS_mtk_eth_soc.o += -O2
+CFLAGS_mtk_ppe.o += -O2
 mtk_eth-$(CONFIG_NET_MEDIATEK_SOC_WED) += mtk_wed.o mtk_wed_mcu.o mtk_wed_wo.o
 ifdef CONFIG_DEBUG_FS
 mtk_eth-$(CONFIG_NET_MEDIATEK_SOC_WED) += mtk_wed_debugfs.o
